  "markdown_content": "## Economic Challenges\\n\\nJapan must embrace increased immigration levels to regain its former economic power, according to a prominent foreign-born CEO operating in the country. The statement comes amid growing concerns about Japan's aging population and shrinking workforce.\\n\\nThe business leader's comments address a critical challenge facing the world's third-largest economy, as it grapples with demographic decline and the need for economic revitalization.\\n\\n## Official Response\\n\\nNewsweek has sought comment from the Japanese Foreign Ministry regarding these statements, reflecting the sensitivity and importance of the immigration debate in Japanese policy circles.",
